# Opt-in (./install.sh --kwallet): use KDE Wallet as the Secret Service.
#
# Apps that store passwords (browsers, NetworkManager agents, …) ask D-Bus for
# org.freedesktop.secrets. If nothing holds that name yet, D-Bus starts
# whatever this file says. Fedora's system copy starts gnome-keyring, so under
# Hyprland the first app to ask can win the race against KWallet's autostart.
# This user copy (~/.local/share/dbus-1/services/) overrides it: ksecretd
# serves org.freedesktop.Secret.Service from your kdewallet.
#
# GNOME/Plasma sessions start their own keyring first, so this only matters
# when nothing has claimed the name yet (e.g. Hyprland).
[D-BUS Service]
Name=org.freedesktop.secrets
Exec=/usr/bin/ksecretd
